        "weight": 800,
        "tracking": 1.4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "t21",
      "page": 1,
      "x": 0.97,
      "y": 8.47,
      "w": 1.76,
      "z": 7,
      "md": "Raise rates on high-value and non-owner-occupied properties, and dedicate the new revenue to Hawaiian Home Lands.",
      "style": {
        "font": "Poppins",
        "size": 12,
        "color": "#253551",
        "leading": 1.38
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "t22",
      "page": 1,
      "x": 3.42,
      "y": 8.47,
      "w": 1.76,
      "z": 7,
      "md": "Extend the earned income, food/excise, and child and dependent care tax credits before they expire.",
      "style": {
        "font": "Poppins",
        "size": 12,
        "color": "#253551",
        "leading": 1.38
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "t23",
      "page": 1,
      "x": 5.87,
      "y": 8.47,
      "w": 1.76,
      "z": 7,
      "md": "Tax capital gains at the same rates as ordinary income, so investment income does not receive preferential treatment.",
      "style": {
        "font": "Poppins",
        "size": 12,
        "color": "#253551",
        "leading": 1.38
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "t15",
      "page": 1,
      "x": 0.97,
      "y": 5.78,
      "w": 1.88,
      "z": 8,
      "md": "Rates **unchanged since 2009**; none of the revenue goes to Hawaiian Home Lands.",
      "style": {
        "font": "Poppins",
        "size": 11,
        "color": "#4A5568",
        "leading": 1.42
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "t16",
      "page": 1,
      "x": 0.97,
      "y": 6.47,
      "w": 1.88,
      "z": 8,
      "md": "Today one rate applies to the **whole price**, so the tax jumps at set prices.",
      "style": {
        "font": "Poppins",
        "size": 11,
        "color": "#4A5568",
        "leading": 1.42
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "t17",
      "page": 1,
      "x": 0.97,
      "y": 7.16,
      "w": 1.88,
      "z": 8,
      "md": "**The proposal:** switch to **marginal rates**, like income tax brackets, so each rate applies only to the part of the price in that bracket.",
      "style": {
        "font": "Poppins",
        "size": 11,
        "color": "#4A5568",
        "leading": 1.42
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "t25",
      "page": 1,
      "x": 3.42,
      "y": 5.78,
      "w": 1.88,
      "z": 8,
      "md": "Act 163 expanded the earned income, food/excise, and child and dependent care credits; all expansions end after 2027.",
      "style": {
        "font": "Poppins",
        "size": 11,
        "color": "#4A5568",
        "leading": 1.42
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "t26",
      "page": 1,
      "x": 3.42,
      "y": 6.52,
      "w": 1.88,
      "z": 8,
      "md": "In 2028, roughly 175,000–185,000 households would get reduced benefits. Single parents would lose $817 on average.",
      "style": {
        "font": "Poppins",
        "size": 11,
        "color": "#4A5568",
        "leading": 1.42
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "t28",
      "page": 1,
      "x": 5.87,
      "y": 5.78,
      "w": 1.88,
      "z": 8,
      "md": "Capital gains are the profits from selling stocks, bonds, and other assets are **taxed at a maximum of 7.25%**; wages are taxed up to **13%**.",
      "style": {
        "font": "Poppins",
        "size": 11,
        "color": "#4A5568",
        "leading": 1.42
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "t30",
      "page": 1,
      "x": 5.87,
      "y": 6.68,
      "w": 1.88,
      "z": 8,
      "md": "**Most local families would pay not pay higher taxes if the capital gains rate were raised.**",
      "style": {
        "font": "Poppins",
        "size": 11,
        "color": "#4A5568",
        "leading": 1.42
      }
    },
    {
